WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.725
Idea. Shops are packed in good years and quiet in bad years. A country's output rises and falls like a wave, again and again.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:22.421
On the diagram, real G D P goes up the side and time along the bottom. The wavy line is actual G D P. The straight dashed line is the trend, the long-run average growth path.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.141
Boom sits at the top of the wave, the peak, where output is highest.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:39.195
Downturn comes just after the peak. Growth slows: G D P is still growing, but more slowly. On the diagram it is the stretch where the line turns down after the peak.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:50.224
Recession is at the bottom of the wave, the trough. Output has fallen for two quarters in a row and is at its lowest. Slump or depression are also accepted.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.471
Recovery is the rising stretch after the trough, where output grows again.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:09.873
Method. Step one, find the label already given. Step two, follow the order left to right: boom, downturn, recession, recovery. Step three, anchor boom at a peak and recession at a trough.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:19.901
Step four, fill the in-between stretches: downturn on the way down, recovery on the way up. Step five, check nothing is repeated or missing.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:35.491
Worked example. Here is a real question from January 2023. The diagram shows real G D P against time, with Boom already labelled at the peak. Label the other three stages. Three marks.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:41.029
Move right from the peak. The line starts to fall, so that box is downturn.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.428
The lowest point of the wave is the trough. Label it recession.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:59.537
After the trough the line climbs again. Label it recovery. Check the order: boom, downturn, recession, recovery. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:09.363
Common mistake. A common mistake is swapping downturn and recovery. Downturn is on the way down. Recovery is on the way up.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.411
Another is calling the trough a downturn, or writing the given label again.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:30.674
Your turn. Now you try. A diagram has recession labelled at the trough. Three empty boxes sit on the rising stretch after it, at the next peak, and on the falling stretch after that peak. Label them. Pause and decide.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.022
Answer. After recession comes recovery, on the rising stretch.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.599
The next peak is boom. The falling stretch after it is downturn.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:49.841
Remember: start from the given label, follow the order, and put boom at peaks and recession at troughs. Now try the practice questions.
